proposed_solution.text:
Use the exponential generating function identity
\[
\sum_{r\ge0}(a)_r\frac{z^r}{r!}=(1-z)^{-a}
\]
and \(\sum_{k\ge0}S(k,r)\frac{x^k}{k!}=\frac{(e^x-1)^r}{r!}\). With \(z=-(e^x-1)\), this gives
\[
\sum_{k\ge0}\left(\sum_{r=0}^{k}(-1)^r(a)_rS(k,r)\right)\frac{x^k}{k!}
=\sum_{r\ge0}(-1)^r(a)_r\frac{(e^x-1)^r}{r!}
=e^{-ax}.
\]

